Produce a final, structured output for the Email Router project.

Reviewer Note

Your output files (agentic_workflow_output.txt and the step_X_output.txt files) indicate that your action_planning_agent is generating 10 highly granular project management steps (e.g., "Set up project repository," "Assign resources," and "Gather feedback").

Because the workflow iterates through 10 generic steps, the final output becomes fragmented. We end up with a mix of ad hoc responses rather than a clean, consolidated list of:

Validated User Stories
Validated Product Features
Validated Engineering Tasks
🛠️ How to resolve this:
We need to constrain the Action Planning Agent so that it generates exactly three steps that our downstream agents are specialized to handle.

You mentioned updating the workflow_prompt (lines 243-246). To resolve this issue, make the prompt even more explicit and restrictive.

Change your workflow_prompt in agentic_workflow.py to something like this:

    workflow_prompt = (
        "Based on the Email Router product spec, generate exactly THREE action steps: "
        "1. Define the user stories. "
        "2. Group the user stories into product features. "
        "3. Define detailed engineering development tasks for those features. "
        "Do not generate any other project management steps."
    )
(Alternatively, you can simplify the knowledge_action_planning variable on line 27 to force the agent to output only those three steps.)

Once your Action Planner outputs exactly 3 steps, your workflow will run smoothly, the Router will send those 3 steps to your 3 expert agents, and your final output will perfectly match the rubric's structural requirements! 🎯

